{# proof.md.j2 — the skeleton for notes/gen/proofs/<NNN>.md.

   One hand-written skeleton owns the mechanical surface of a proof-level
   faithfulness audit page; a per-family data file (notes/data/proofs/<NNN>.md)
   supplies the section bodies with quote tokens. The renderer (build_proofs.py)
   composes them, resolving each quote through the same path
   build_summaries.resolve_token uses for summary pages.

   Proof audits are family-shaped — the set of `## sections` one audit carries
   is not a fixed canonical set the way the summary sections are (091 has
   statement / l_p / proof structure / dimension handling / …, 072 has
   statement / sign convention / sign audit / …). The template renders
   whichever sections the data file carries, in the order it carries them,
   and then the fixed `## Sources` table.
#}
